WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.168
JESSIE HOLMES (VOICEOVER):
What doesn't kill

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.636
you just makes you stronger.

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.339
Good practice, get knocked
down, get right back up again

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.207
and get back to work.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.676
[music playing]

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.586
JESSIE HOLMES: Gee,
gee, gee, gee, gee.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:27.394
Just got the dogs
out for a good run.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.962
I'm about to start
working on my cabin.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.798
It's kind of been getting
put off a long time.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.299
Had a lot of other
stuff on the plate,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.003
but the tent's kind of becoming
undesirable to live in,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.941
and winter is
extremely set in here.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.977
Winter's long, but
the daylight's short.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.613
And it's been some 20,
25 below temperatures,

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.249
and now the temperatures
are really starting to drop.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.952
Nothing like some deep,
cold to get some urgency.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:57.457
Started this cabin, you know,
before the snow started flying.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.992
I've got everything sealed in.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.695
I got a solid roof on it,
solid foundation, solid walls,

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:07.667
but what I need to do right
now is get the roof insulated.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.470
The daylight's about to be gone.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.939
Limited daylight is
about four hours.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:18.311
If I work four hours a day,
nothing's going to get done.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.747
So I mean, I could be cutting
wood at 3:00 in the morning,

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.215
running dogs 3:00
in the morning,

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.918
building the cabin at 3:00 in
the morning, whatever it takes.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.193
You getting this cabin
bill just in time,

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.328
cold's really starting
to move in here.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.834
Got the first sheet cut here.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.336
This is one of those things
it would be real nice to have

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:47.574
a second hand with, but this is
where years of handling plywood

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.374
comes into play.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.680
This is going to be the
part that's not very fun.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.087
Thank God I got some
purchase on that one.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.428
Whenever I was 20 years
old living in a tent,

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.863
all winter was nothing.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.631
But I'm not 20
years old anymore.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.465
I don't recover.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.100
I don't bounce back as quick.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.468
A person needs to feel human.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.337
They need a place
to have their own,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:22.242
be dry, be warm, keep all
their most important things out

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.009
of the weather.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.448
It feels good to get
some momentum back

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.582
into this project.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:33.019
The hardest thing is to
get going, sometimes.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.988
If you're going to be efficient
and effective out here,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.789
you have to figure
out ways of killing

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.224
two birds with one stone.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.928
You've got to think
multi-dimensional.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.564
OK, I got most of my
plywood up on the ceiling.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.033
This area I need to leave open,
because I'm going to start

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.768
setting my stove up here.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:52.005
This is kind of
the exciting part.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.573
I'm really looking forward
to getting this wood

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.774
stove in here,
because then I can

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.609
get myself a source of heat.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.912
I mean, I've been living
in a tent all winter.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:02.682
I'm out here working in the cold
all night because I want to get

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:06.052
this done, get this cabin
good enough that I can start

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.621
moving my stuff in it tonight.

